concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3f a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "3F The things authorised by a search warrant—general"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-3f ;
    values:originalText "(1) A warrant that is in force in relation to premises authorises the executing officer or a constable assisting:  (a) to enter the warrant premises and, if the premises are a conveyance, to enter the conveyance, wherever it is; and  (b) to search for and record fingerprints found at the premises and to take samples of things found at the premises for forensic purposes; and  (c) to search the premises for the kinds of evidential material specified in the warrant, and to seize things of that kind found at the premises; and   Part IAA  Search, information gathering, arrest and related powers (other than powers under delayed notification search warrants)" ;
    skos:definition "(1) A warrant that is in force in relation to premises authorises the executing officer or a constable assisting:  (a) to enter the warrant premises and, if the premises are a conveyance, to enter the conveyance, wherever it is; and  (b) to search for and record fingerprints found at the premises and to take samples of things found at the premises for forensic purposes; and  (c) to search the premises for the kinds of evidential material specified in the warrant, and to seize things of that kind found at the premises; and   Part IAA  Search, information gathering, arrest and related powers (other than powers under delayed notification search warrants)"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "1288d9274f6dce1e2cf99171426d99dda44e621da04419fa8a42542366fef991" ;
    cof:pageNumber "43"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Restricts entry and search of premises without warrant." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <crimes-act-1914.pdf> ;
    dc:source "crimes-act-1914.pdf, p.43" ;
    cml:asserts concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3f-norm .
