concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3ud-ss-4 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "3UD(4) Stopping and searching"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-3ud-ss-4 ;
    values:originalText "(4) In searching a thing (including a vehicle) under subsection (1), a police officer may use such force as is reasonable and necessary in the circumstances, but must not damage the thing by forcing it, or a part of it, open unless:   Part IAA  Search, information gathering, arrest and related powers (other than powers under delayed notification search warrants)" ;
    skos:definition "(4) In searching a thing (including a vehicle) under subsection (1), a police officer may use such force as is reasonable and necessary in the circumstances, but must not damage the thing by forcing it, or a part of it, open unless:   Part IAA  Search, information gathering, arrest and related powers (other than powers under delayed notification search warrants)"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "1fb43c0cd013a679cc5f27f4460ac98c3fbab6079607e02e0f44a42ccc98c03f" ;
    values:partOf concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3ud ;
    cof:pageNumber "80"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Police officer must not damage thing by forcing it open unless certain conditions are met." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
