concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3uo a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "3UO Determination of airports"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-3uo ;
    values:originalText "(1) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, determine an airport for the purposes of the definition of major airport in section 3UM.  (2) A determination of an airport under subsection (1) must include a description of land in relation to the airport for the purposes of paragraph 3UM(2)(b).  (3) This Division applies in relation to an airport determined under subsection (1) only if the airport is ordinarily used for the purposes of any of the following:  (a) flights that start or end in a Territory;  (b) flights between Australia and a foreign country in which aircraft are used in the course of trade or commerce, for the carriage of passengers;  (c) flights between one State and another State in which aircraft are used in the course of trade or commerce, for the carriage of passengers.  (4) This Division may apply in relation to an airport determined under subsection (1) even if the airport is also used for a purpose other than a purpose mentioned in subsection (3). Note: See also section 3UR (move-on directions at airports—alternative constitutional scope).   Search, information gathering, arrest and related powers (other than powers under delayed notification search warrants)  Part IAA Identity information requirements, and move-on powers, at airports  Division 3B  Section 3UP  Crimes Act 1914  Compilation date: 04/06/2026" ;
    skos:definition "(1) The Minister may, by legislative instrument, determine an airport for the purposes of the definition of major airport in section 3UM.  (2) A determination of an airport under subsection (1) must include a description of land in relation to the airport for the purposes of paragraph 3UM(2)(b).  (3) This Division applies in relation to an airport determined under subsection (1) only if the airport is ordinarily used for the purposes of any of the following:  (a) flights that start or end in a Territory;  (b) flights between Australia and a foreign country in which aircraft are used in the course of trade or commerce, for the carriage of passengers;  (c) flights between one State and another State in which aircraft are used in the course of trade or commerce, for the carriage of passengers.  (4) This Division may apply in relation to an airport determined under subsection (1) even if the airport is also used for a purpose other than a purpose mentioned in subsection (3). Note: See also section 3UR (move-on directions at airports—alternative constitutional scope).   Search, information gathering, arrest and related powers (other than powers under delayed notification search warrants)  Part IAA Identity information requirements, and move-on powers, at airports  Division 3B  Section 3UP  Crimes Act 1914  Compilation date: 04/06/2026"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "1147a8754dd20e6c0f73c6614e420235e4c315b7617856221a150346d34d5fe4" ;
    cof:pageNumber "100"^^xsd:integer ;
