doc:sec-3ur a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "3UR Move-on directions at airports—alternative constitutional" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "scope  Without limiting its effect apart from this section, section 3UQ also has the effect it would have if the definition of major airport in section 3UM did not include an airport determined by the Minister under section 3UO." ;
    cof:pageNumber "104"^^xsd:integer .

concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3us a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "3US Stop and directions powers at airports"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-3us ;
    values:originalText "(1) A constable or a protective service officer may give a person a direction under this section if:  (a) the direction is given at a major airport; and  (b) the constable or officer considers on reasonable grounds that it is necessary to give the direction to facilitate the exercise of a power under section 3UP (identity information at airports) or section 3UQ (move-on directions at airports).  (2) The constable or officer may direct the person:  (a) to stop; or  (b) to do anything else the constable or officer considers on reasonable grounds to be necessary to facilitate the exercise of a power under section 3UP or 3UQ.   Search, information gathering, arrest and related powers (other than powers under delayed notification search warrants)  Part IAA Identity information requirements, and move-on powers, at airports  Division 3B  Section 3UT  Crimes Act 1914  Compilation date: 04/06/2026" ;
    skos:definition "(1) A constable or a protective service officer may give a person a direction under this section if:  (a) the direction is given at a major airport; and  (b) the constable or officer considers on reasonable grounds that it is necessary to give the direction to facilitate the exercise of a power under section 3UP (identity information at airports) or section 3UQ (move-on directions at airports).  (2) The constable or officer may direct the person:  (a) to stop; or  (b) to do anything else the constable or officer considers on reasonable grounds to be necessary to facilitate the exercise of a power under section 3UP or 3UQ.   Search, information gathering, arrest and related powers (other than powers under delayed notification search warrants)  Part IAA Identity information requirements, and move-on powers, at airports  Division 3B  Section 3UT  Crimes Act 1914  Compilation date: 04/06/2026"@en ;
