concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3zc-ss-2 cml:asserts concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3zc-ss-2-logic-deontic-4 .
concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3zc-ss-2-logic-deontic-4 a cml:LogicApplication ;
    cml:modality cml:Deontic ;
    cml:operator "forbid" ;
    cml:logicSummary "Prohibition of using force to cause harm during escape" ;
    cml:premiseText "(b) if the person is attempting to escape arrest by fleeing—do such a thing unless:" ;
    cml:conclusionText "...unless:  (i) the constable believes on reasonable grounds that doing that thing is necessary to protect life or to prevent serious injury to another person (including the constable); and" ;
    cml:executionSurface "modalities::logic::deontic" ;
    cml:confidence "1.0000"^^xsd:decimal ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed .
doc:sec-3zc-ss-2 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "3ZC(2) Use of force in making arrest" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(2) Without limiting the operation of subsection (1), a constable must not, in the course of arresting a person for an offence:  (a) do anything that is likely to cause the death of, or grievous bodily harm to, the person unless the constable believes on reasonable grounds that doing that thing is necessary to protect life or to prevent serious injury to another person (including the constable); or  (b) if the person is attempting to escape arrest by fleeing—do such a thing unless:  (i) the constable believes on reasonable grounds that doing that thing is necessary to protect life or to prevent serious injury to another person (including the constable); and  (ii) the person has, if practicable, been called on to surrender and the constable believes on reasonable grounds that the person cannot be apprehended in any other manner." ;
    cof:pageNumber "115"^^xsd:integer .

concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3zd a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "3ZD Persons to be informed of grounds of arrest"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-3zd ;
    values:originalText "(1) A person who arrests another person for an offence must inform the other person, at the time of the arrest, of the offence for which the other person is being arrested.  (2) It is sufficient if the other person is informed of the substance of the offence, and it is not necessary that this be done in language of a precise or technical nature.  (3) Subsection (1) does not apply to the arrest of the other person if:   Part IAA  Search, information gathering, arrest and related powers (other than powers under delayed notification search warrants)" ;
    skos:definition "(1) A person who arrests another person for an offence must inform the other person, at the time of the arrest, of the offence for which the other person is being arrested.  (2) It is sufficient if the other person is informed of the substance of the offence, and it is not necessary that this be done in language of a precise or technical nature.  (3) Subsection (1) does not apply to the arrest of the other person if:   Part IAA  Search, information gathering, arrest and related powers (other than powers under delayed notification search warrants)"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "299e64b58ae2cbad1b1e4f8eedc0e52f619f08fe6cc6a276651cea10c2ae3069" ;
    cof:pageNumber "115"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3zd-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3zd-ss-2 ;
