concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-3zj-ss-7 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "3ZJ(7) Taking fingerprints, recordings, samples of handwriting or"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-3zj-ss-7 ;
    values:originalText "(7) In deciding whether to make such an order, the magistrate must have regard to:  (a) the seriousness of the offence; and  (b) the age or any disability of the person; and  (c) such other matters as the magistrate thinks fit." ;
    skos:definition "(7) In deciding whether to make such an order, the magistrate must have regard to:  (a) the seriousness of the offence; and  (b) the age or any disability of the person; and  (c) such other matters as the magistrate thinks fit."@en ;
