    skos:prefLabel "4AB Conversion of pecuniary penalties expressed in dollar amounts"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-4ab ;
    values:originalText "to penalty units  (1) A reference in a law of the Commonwealth or in a Territory Ordinance to a pecuniary penalty of D dollars, where D is a number, is taken to be a reference to a pecuniary penalty of P penalty units, where P is:  (a) if D   100 is a whole number—that whole number; or  (b) if D   100 is not a whole number—the next highest whole number.  (2) Subsection (1) does not apply to a reference to the maximum amount of a penalty that is not imposed by a court, or by a service tribunal under the Defence Force Discipline Act 1982.  (3) Subsection (1) does not apply to:  (a) section 76 of the Competition and Consumer Act 2010; or  (c) a provision of a law of the Commonwealth prescribed for the purposes of this subsection.  (4) In this section: penalty includes a fine. Territory Ordinance has the same meaning as in section 4AA." ;
    skos:definition "to penalty units  (1) A reference in a law of the Commonwealth or in a Territory Ordinance to a pecuniary penalty of D dollars, where D is a number, is taken to be a reference to a pecuniary penalty of P penalty units, where P is:  (a) if D   100 is a whole number—that whole number; or  (b) if D   100 is not a whole number—the next highest whole number.  (2) Subsection (1) does not apply to a reference to the maximum amount of a penalty that is not imposed by a court, or by a service tribunal under the Defence Force Discipline Act 1982.  (3) Subsection (1) does not apply to:  (a) section 76 of the Competition and Consumer Act 2010; or  (c) a provision of a law of the Commonwealth prescribed for the purposes of this subsection.  (4) In this section: penalty includes a fine. Territory Ordinance has the same meaning as in section 4AA."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "bca2c22445edafec619227394a73cfbb7e24503f92e4c1b02187f331304a95b6" ;
