doc:sec-4m a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "4M Children under 10" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "A child under 10 years old cannot be liable for an offence against a law of the Commonwealth." ;
    cof:pageNumber "337"^^xsd:integer .

concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-4n a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "4N Children over 10 but under 14"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-4n ;
    values:originalText "(1) A child aged 10 years or more but under 14 years old can only be liable for an offence against a law of the Commonwealth if the child knows that his or her conduct is wrong.  (2) The question whether a child knows that his or her conduct is wrong is one of fact. The burden of proving this is on the prosecution." ;
