concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-9 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "9 Seizure and condemnation of forfeitable goods"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-9 ;
    values:originalText "(1) Any constable may, without warrant, seize any articles which are forfeited or which he or she has reasonable ground to believe are forfeited under any law of the Commonwealth, and take them before a court of summary jurisdiction.  (2) Where articles are taken before a court of summary jurisdiction under subsection (1), the court shall inquire into the matter and:  (a) if the court is satisfied that the articles are forfeited—shall order that the articles be condemned; or  (b) if the court is not so satisfied—shall order that the articles be delivered to such person as the court is satisfied is entitled to the articles." ;
    skos:definition "(1) Any constable may, without warrant, seize any articles which are forfeited or which he or she has reasonable ground to believe are forfeited under any law of the Commonwealth, and take them before a court of summary jurisdiction.  (2) Where articles are taken before a court of summary jurisdiction under subsection (1), the court shall inquire into the matter and:  (a) if the court is satisfied that the articles are forfeited—shall order that the articles be condemned; or  (b) if the court is not so satisfied—shall order that the articles be delivered to such person as the court is satisfied is entitled to the articles."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "a6d23416a667121ac2e986c470c05733b738fafffc9e66dbad02dbac08a3e072" ;
    cof:pageNumber "337"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-9-ss-1 ;
