concept:crimes-act-1914-sec-9b a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "9B Costs etc. payable to Official Trustee"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-9b ;
    values:originalText "(1) The regulations may make provision in relation to:  (a) the costs, charges and expenses incurred in connection with; and  (b) the Official Trustee’s remuneration in respect of; the performance or exercise by the Official Trustee of functions, duties or powers under section 9A.   General  Part IA  Section 13  Crimes Act 1914  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  (2) An amount equal to each amount of remuneration that the Official Trustee receives under the regulations is to be paid to the Commonwealth.  (3) Where there are no regulations in relation to a matter referred to in subsection (1):  (a) the regulations referred to in section 288 of the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002 apply, so far as they are applicable, and with appropriate changes, in relation to the matter; and  (b) a reference in subsection (1) or (2) to regulations is taken to be a reference to the regulations referred to in section 288 of the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002." ;
    skos:definition "(1) The regulations may make provision in relation to:  (a) the costs, charges and expenses incurred in connection with; and  (b) the Official Trustee’s remuneration in respect of; the performance or exercise by the Official Trustee of functions, duties or powers under section 9A.   General  Part IA  Section 13  Crimes Act 1914  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  (2) An amount equal to each amount of remuneration that the Official Trustee receives under the regulations is to be paid to the Commonwealth.  (3) Where there are no regulations in relation to a matter referred to in subsection (1):  (a) the regulations referred to in section 288 of the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002 apply, so far as they are applicable, and with appropriate changes, in relation to the matter; and  (b) a reference in subsection (1) or (2) to regulations is taken to be a reference to the regulations referred to in section 288 of the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "7579f5f9993d05196249eb2bf1a041873a92cfb9746fdfb8445b1de920584904" ;
    cof:pageNumber "338"^^xsd:integer ;
